{"kind":"request","text":"Security R15 (one-channel audit 1e8ef5d5, disposition D5): a retired hosted agent can still sign.\n\nFound at main c40492ee. The hosted endpoint's retire control sets the agent row to `retired`, clears its bearer and deletes its sessions (packages/mcp/src/hosted.ts:517-520). It does not revoke the agent's key in membership, and it keeps the agent's private seed (hosted.ts:305, :403-408). The key stays active. Anyone or anything that holds the seed can still sign acts as that agent, and the room's record shows no end for the agent.\n\nWork:\n1. Retire ends the key in the record. After a retire, membership shows the agent's key revoked (`revoke-key`, as: retired), by a recorded act. Choose the signer that membership admits: the agent's own key revoking itself before its seed is deleted, or the controller's signed revoke carried with the retire control. Say which in the head report.\n2. Retire deletes the seed. After a retire, the endpoint holds no private seed for the agent, and no later control can sign with it.\n3. Order and failure. A retire is not reported complete until membership shows the key revoked and the seed is gone. If the revoke is refused or uncertain, the retire answer says so, the agent stays unable to act through the endpoint, and a retry finishes the same retire. It never signs a second, different revoke.\n4. Documentation: docs/mcp.md says what retire does to the key, the seed and the record.\n\nBearer plaintext in stored control answers is R5's item 5 (8a856f92) and is not repeated here.\n\nWitnesses:\n- An agent enrolled through the endpoint signs an act, then is retired. An act signed afterwards with its key is refused because the key is revoked, both at the endpoint and when submitted directly to the scope.\n- After retire, the endpoint's storage holds no seed for the agent (a direct store probe).\n- A retire whose revoke is refused leaves the agent unable to act through the endpoint and reports the refusal; a retry completes it.\n- Replay of the membership journal shows the revoke entry.\n\nPlace in the security order: with R5 (8a856f92), in the same head or the next one. The archive items keep priority (F3 8fda2549, step 6 7b19837c).","body":{"conditions":"Retire revokes the agent's key by a recorded act and deletes its seed; retire completes only when both hold; witnesses at the endpoint, at the scope, in storage and in replay. Checker review on every head; one gate at the final head; hosted Workers stay deployable; no builder deployment. Security order: with R5.","target":"inherit","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}